    </div>

    <section class="intro">
      <h2>What a Restaurant Manager Really Owns</h2>
      <p>A Restaurant Manager&#8217;s job is bigger than the floor. It spans operations, people, guest experience, compliance, and the numbers &#8212; all at once, every shift. Here&#8217;s the full breakdown of what the role actually covers.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="breakdown">
      <h2>1. Operations Management</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Oversee the day-to-day operations of the restaurant</li>
        <li>Ensure smooth execution of all shifts and maintain high service standards</li>
        <li>Manage inventory, cash handling, daily reports, and deposits</li>
        <li>Control labor costs, food costs, waste, and overall restaurant profitability</li>
        <li>Monitor operational KPIs and implement improvements</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. Team Leadership</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Recruit, train, coach, and develop team members</li>
        <li>Prepare staff rosters and ensure adequate manpower</li>
        <li>Conduct daily briefings and performance reviews</li>
        <li>Motivate the team to achieve sales and guest satisfaction targets</li>
        <li>Resolve employee concerns and maintain a positive work environment</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Guest Experience</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Deliver exceptional customer service</li>
        <li>Handle guest complaints professionally and ensure prompt resolution</li>
        <li>Build guest relationships to encourage repeat business</li>
        <li>Monitor guest feedback and improve service standards</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Compliance &amp; Safety</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Ensure compliance with food safety, hygiene, sanitation, and health regulations</li>
        <li>Enforce company policies, security procedures, and workplace safety standards</li>
        <li>Maintain audit readiness and ensure legal compliance</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Financial &amp; Business Management</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Achieve sales, profitability, and budget targets</li>
        <li>Analyze daily sales reports and identify growth opportunities</li>
        <li>Control food cost, beverage cost, and operating expenses</li>
        <li>Drive local store marketing and promotional activities to increase revenue</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

